     5	/**
     6	 * Identity & Attestation — Ed25519 key lifecycle as a first-class concern.
     7	 *
     8	 *  - issue: mint a keypair with tight expiry (default 1h, hard cap 24h)
     9	 *  - rotate: mark the current key revoked, mint the next — old key stays
    10	 *    verifiable for in-flight settlements
    11	 *  - sign: http-message-signatures style signature over selected headers
    12	 *  - PACT: broker-issued attestation token the origin can verify against
    13	 *    the public directory
    14	 *
    15	 * The directory payload below is what the broker serves at
    16	 * `/.well-known/agent-identity` so origins can look up the public key
    17	 * without a side channel.
    18	 *
    19	 * Draft-caveat discipline: build against the *patterns* of Web Bot Auth
    20	 * and PACT, not their draft field names.
    21	 */
    22	
    23	export type B64Url = string;
    24	
    25	/**
    26	 * A minimal JSON Web Key shape for an OKP / Ed25519 key. The broker never
    27	 * needs the full JWK surface — only the fields it round-trips through
